WEBVTT

00:16.440 --> 00:17.816
What the heck?

00:21.695 --> 00:24.489
No, wait! You can't prove who did it.

00:24.573 --> 00:25.574
MANATSU ATAGAWA

00:25.657 --> 00:27.701
Who else would do this
but that dang Atagawa!

00:28.577 --> 00:31.997
Atagawa...

00:32.080 --> 00:33.081
What?

00:34.374 --> 00:37.919
Did you not learn in elementary school
that trash goes in the trash can?

00:38.003 --> 00:39.004
Miki!

00:40.255 --> 00:41.339
Don't know what you're on about.

00:41.923 --> 00:43.300
You damn well do!

00:43.383 --> 00:44.384
Let go of me!

00:47.846 --> 00:49.931
<i>I never noticed.</i>

00:52.309 --> 00:53.727
Why didn't you run for it?

00:54.394 --> 00:56.855
I mean, maybe you could have
gotten it, Miki, but...

00:56.938 --> 00:58.523
Don't give me that!

00:58.607 --> 01:01.568
There's a difference between not being
able to get it and just giving up.

01:01.651 --> 01:05.280
<i>I never realized
clearly expressing my opinions</i>

01:05.363 --> 01:07.908
<i>could cause anguish in others.</i>

01:08.992 --> 01:10.994
Isn't being liked good enough?

01:11.078 --> 01:12.329
Asking for more is greedy.

01:12.412 --> 01:15.999
<i>I never realized
when I hurt my dear friend.</i>

01:19.878 --> 01:21.671
<i>The more I spoke up,</i>

01:22.380 --> 01:24.007
<i>the more I acted,</i>

01:25.133 --> 01:27.135
<i>the more I was just running in place.</i>

01:34.518 --> 01:36.394
<i>I won't say more than is necessary.</i>

01:36.895 --> 01:39.231
<i>Don't make a fuss. Don't shout.</i>

01:39.981 --> 01:41.900
<i>Don't hurt others.</i>

01:43.318 --> 01:44.319
All right.

01:45.987 --> 01:49.366
Hey, would you like
to walk to the next class with us?

01:49.449 --> 01:51.993
Huh? Oh, sure.

01:52.077 --> 01:53.411
Hooray!

01:54.037 --> 01:58.125
<i>I decided to pay extra attention
to not making any missteps in high school.</i>

01:58.208 --> 02:02.921
I'd been thinking to myself,
"Wow, this girl in class is so pretty."

02:04.005 --> 02:08.385
<i>And since I made that decision,
things have been going scarily smooth.</i>

02:09.177 --> 02:12.013
Hey. Tsu-kun's gonna be
in that upcoming movie.

02:12.097 --> 02:14.266
That live-adaptation from the manga?

02:14.349 --> 02:17.394
Which manga? I read quite a lot.

02:17.477 --> 02:18.478
SHONEN GANG

02:18.562 --> 02:19.688
You might know it then.

02:20.438 --> 02:23.692
<i>100 Sunflowers of Love for You</i>.

02:24.317 --> 02:27.070
<i>100? Isn't that a bit much?</i>

02:27.154 --> 02:28.947
HAS NO IDEA WHEN IT COMES
TO GIRLS' MANGA

03:59.746 --> 04:03.959
EPISODE 8
ON EQUAL FOOTING

04:06.127 --> 04:08.463
<i>I kind of had a hunch, but...</i>

04:08.546 --> 04:11.007
<i>Our tastes are totally different.</i>

04:11.091 --> 04:12.717
GRADE 1 CLASS 5

04:12.801 --> 04:14.970
Okay, got it. See you.

04:20.433 --> 04:21.977
LIGHTS UP

04:24.187 --> 04:25.605
Yota! Guess what?

04:26.189 --> 04:28.108
I think I can afford a motorcycle soon.

04:28.191 --> 04:30.110
Wow, congratulations!

04:30.694 --> 04:33.029
I'd love to go somewhere
once it's a bit warmer.

04:33.113 --> 04:35.991
I'd like a valley
with a river or something.

04:36.074 --> 04:37.742
Yes! That sounds awesome!

04:37.826 --> 04:40.203
A local spot with a nice view
is best for a first outing.

04:40.287 --> 04:41.288
OH, MAN! THIS IS AWESOME!

04:41.371 --> 04:42.622
<i>Now this is fun!</i>

04:46.084 --> 04:49.879
If only we could spend every day together.

04:51.715 --> 04:53.383
What are ya talking about?

04:53.466 --> 04:55.051
Hey, Minato.

04:55.135 --> 04:58.263
We were just saying we'd like to go
on a little excursion once it gets warmer.

04:58.346 --> 05:00.473
Wow, sounds rad!

05:03.727 --> 05:06.938
Sorry, it's from a senior.
I'll just go take this.

05:07.772 --> 05:09.649
Okay, I'll be going too.

05:12.444 --> 05:14.279
Miki. Wait.

05:15.905 --> 05:17.198
I...

05:18.033 --> 05:20.702
Could you tell me more about Hikawa?

05:21.911 --> 05:23.038
Come again?

05:23.705 --> 05:25.081
In what way this time?

05:25.165 --> 05:26.791
Well, I mean...

05:27.292 --> 05:30.337
I just wanna, like,
be good friends with her.

05:31.504 --> 05:35.467
Like, what does she like?
What doesn't she like?

05:35.550 --> 05:38.470
Don't you worry. You'll get there.

05:38.553 --> 05:40.347
Just be yourself.

05:40.430 --> 05:43.308
I mean, what's most important
is acting from the heart. Am I right?

05:43.391 --> 05:44.851
You're being very abstract.

05:45.560 --> 05:49.105
- Did you see that? That was amazing.
- Yeah.

05:49.189 --> 05:50.523
100 SUNFLOWERS OF LOVE FOR YOU 1

05:50.607 --> 05:52.609
That was just like out of <i>100 Sunflowers</i>.

05:54.277 --> 05:55.445
Wait up.

05:57.280 --> 05:58.281
Miki.

05:58.364 --> 05:59.657
Minato.

06:00.950 --> 06:04.829
Hey, Miki. What's up with you and Amamiya?

06:05.997 --> 06:07.165
<i>What?</i>

06:07.248 --> 06:09.626
- You two looked so good together just now.
- Yeah.

06:09.709 --> 06:10.919
Just now?

06:11.753 --> 06:13.463
No, it's not like that.

06:13.546 --> 06:16.716
But you're also pretty close
with Hino too, aren't you?

06:16.800 --> 06:19.385
You're right!
I see them talking every now and then.

06:19.469 --> 06:21.721
Which one do you actually like?

06:21.805 --> 06:23.723
I'm telling you. It's not like that!

06:26.810 --> 06:29.687
I mean, we're just friends, so...

06:30.188 --> 06:31.189
PLOD PLOD

06:31.272 --> 06:32.899
I'm sorry.

06:34.109 --> 06:38.113
She seemed much happier
talking to the boys just now.

06:39.989 --> 06:44.327
<i>Why say such things
when we were just having a chat?</i>

06:44.410 --> 06:46.412
<i>I feel so sorry for the guys.</i>

06:46.913 --> 06:49.999
<i>Nobody would have said anything
if we were all back in middle school.</i>

06:50.667 --> 06:53.711
<i>You were born in the wrong body, Azumi.</i>

06:53.795 --> 06:55.046
Yeah!

06:55.130 --> 06:57.257
<i>Is it because none of them
actually saw me as a girl?</i>

06:57.340 --> 06:59.092
TOO SCARED TO SPEAK UP

06:59.175 --> 07:00.176
MIKI, YOU'RE SO BLUNT

07:00.260 --> 07:02.178
<i>I'm trying not to misstep. So why?</i>

07:02.262 --> 07:03.263
DON'T SAY IT LIKE THAT

07:05.098 --> 07:09.269
I want to break free
from being "cute" and being a "girl"!

07:10.353 --> 07:12.480
- Have a nice evening.
- Good work.

07:13.648 --> 07:14.649
Miki.

07:14.732 --> 07:16.901
Wanna grab a hot drink or something?

07:22.365 --> 07:27.620
So, yeah. I get super nervous
when I'm around a bunch of girly girls.

07:27.704 --> 07:29.914
I've never been good
at reading between the lines.

07:30.498 --> 07:33.251
I'd rather people just say what they mean,

07:33.334 --> 07:35.545
but that got me into trouble
in middle school.

07:35.628 --> 07:39.048
So now I'm trying to be
somebody that I'm not,

07:39.132 --> 07:41.634
but I just can't seem
to strike the right balance.

07:41.718 --> 07:44.429
And now it's like there's no going back.

07:44.512 --> 07:48.516
Also, I wish people would say
I'm "cool" rather than "cute."

07:50.310 --> 07:51.728
Such a teenage thing to say.

07:51.811 --> 07:55.023
Oh, man. I'd forgotten how it feels.

07:55.106 --> 07:58.067
This is actually quite serious for me.

07:58.151 --> 08:04.115
Yeah, it sucks having to live
in a tiny bubble when you're a student.

08:04.199 --> 08:08.703
But life gets way better with more options
once you become an adult.

08:08.786 --> 08:09.787
TOUCHED

08:09.871 --> 08:11.206
Naww, you guys...

08:11.289 --> 08:12.290
CRUSH

08:14.125 --> 08:15.710
Dang, girl! You got grip!

08:16.711 --> 08:17.921
That was insane.

08:19.923 --> 08:24.969
Man, I'll bet class would be a riot
with a girl like you in it.

08:25.053 --> 08:28.973
No way. I'm telling you.
I'm not like this at school.

08:29.474 --> 08:30.683
<i>Miki?</i>

08:32.018 --> 08:33.937
Are you sure?

08:34.020 --> 08:35.230
Yeah.

08:35.313 --> 08:36.481
Now that you mention it,

08:36.564 --> 08:40.235
she doesn't really talk
about herself much, does she?

08:40.944 --> 08:45.490
I've got a friend from cram school who
went to the same middle school as Miki.

08:45.573 --> 08:47.367
She says Miki never picked up
on social cues,

08:47.450 --> 08:48.993
and that she was really abrasive.

08:49.077 --> 08:52.747
She says she tried to punch another girl
and broke glass in the act.

08:52.830 --> 08:55.375
No way. That can't be true.

08:55.875 --> 08:59.379
- But Miki does have that scar.
- What?

08:59.462 --> 09:00.547
Morning!

09:04.509 --> 09:05.510
<i>What?</i>

09:11.182 --> 09:14.435
<i>That was the day
I noticed something was off.</i>

09:14.519 --> 09:17.188
Did you see Tsu-kun's
guest appearance yesterday?

09:17.272 --> 09:18.940
On that talk show?

09:19.023 --> 09:20.692
Wasn't he just the cutest?

09:20.775 --> 09:21.818
Definitely.

09:21.901 --> 09:23.945
Hey, I saw that too.

09:26.030 --> 09:27.031
Well...

09:27.865 --> 09:30.451
<i>They seemed to be keeping
their distance ever since.</i>

09:31.452 --> 09:33.830
<i>I must be overthinking.
It must just be my imagination.</i>

09:34.664 --> 09:37.667
<i>It's so trivial,
and I could just as easily let it go,</i>

09:38.918 --> 09:41.796
<i>but this has happened before,
and so I'm sure of it.</i>

09:43.798 --> 09:47.719
<i>Why must I pick up on things
I'd rather not pick up on?</i>

09:47.802 --> 09:49.470
<i>But what could be causing this?</i>

09:49.554 --> 09:51.472
I'm telling you. It's not like that!

09:52.515 --> 09:54.976
<i>Did I come off too strong?</i>

09:55.059 --> 09:59.188
<i>Or was I being insensitive again
without realizing it?</i>

10:01.357 --> 10:02.900
You're really struggling there.

10:03.776 --> 10:04.902
Ciao!

10:07.071 --> 10:08.656
Minato!

10:08.740 --> 10:10.408
THAT'S NOT THE REACTION
I WAS EXPECTING

10:10.491 --> 10:11.909
<i>Don't surprise me like that!</i>

10:11.993 --> 10:14.078
So what can you not decide on?

10:14.579 --> 10:17.081
Curry? Aojiru? Want me to press for you?

10:17.165 --> 10:19.500
No, I already got an orange juice.

10:19.584 --> 10:22.920
Then we'll do a coin flip.
Heads is curry, tails is aojiru.

10:23.004 --> 10:26.257
I told you, I already got an orange juice.
Oh, my gosh!

10:28.009 --> 10:29.886
My straw fell in.

10:30.553 --> 10:32.430
Why would you put it in
without extending it?

10:32.513 --> 10:35.433
Yota! Your head is so in the clouds.

10:35.516 --> 10:36.643
In the clouds?

10:36.726 --> 10:40.313
<i>This is fun. I feel so at ease.</i>

10:40.396 --> 10:43.441
<i>I don't want to go back to class.</i>

10:43.524 --> 10:46.778
<i>I want to stay here with these two.</i>

10:52.950 --> 10:53.951
Miki.

10:55.912 --> 10:59.582
Honestly, kid. I take my eye off you
for one second and look at what you do.

10:59.666 --> 11:01.918
- You're bothering Azumi!
- No--

11:02.001 --> 11:03.086
I WASN'T HANGING MY HEAD
BECAUSE I WAS BOTHERED...

11:03.169 --> 11:05.463
- Withdraw! Withdraw!
- Apologies!

11:05.546 --> 11:08.091
- Hey, wait!
- Sorry to trouble you!

11:08.174 --> 11:09.842
ALL ALONE

11:09.926 --> 11:12.762
<i>The boys have their own community.</i>

11:13.513 --> 11:16.683
<i>Guess that means
I really don't belong anywhere.</i>

11:17.642 --> 11:18.976
Miki!

11:19.894 --> 11:21.854
I'll be in touch tonight.

11:22.563 --> 11:23.981
Talk to you later.

11:26.317 --> 11:28.736
TOUCHED

11:30.488 --> 11:33.741
You really didn't have to come
all the way over to my place.

11:33.825 --> 11:35.952
It's not far with the motorcycle.

11:36.035 --> 11:39.372
And you'll be able to go far
with your own someday soon too.

11:40.039 --> 11:42.208
I can't wait to go touring together.

11:42.834 --> 11:45.878
Yota. You're too kind.

11:46.462 --> 11:48.214
I'm nothing special.

11:53.719 --> 11:54.971
I...

11:56.305 --> 11:58.641
I think I messed up again.

11:59.350 --> 12:03.729
I've been trying so hard
to be different during high school.

12:05.314 --> 12:06.899
But I can't even do that right.

12:08.860 --> 12:11.404
We all know you're trying.

12:11.988 --> 12:13.948
Koyun knows. Minato knows. And I know.

12:14.615 --> 12:16.993
We all know you.

12:18.244 --> 12:21.998
We know who you are,
and that's why we want to be with you.

12:26.878 --> 12:31.424
I... I feel like I've been
losing sight of who I am lately.

12:36.596 --> 12:39.223
Yota... Thank you.

12:40.892 --> 12:41.976
I love you.

12:45.688 --> 12:49.942
I'm so glad we're friends.

12:52.528 --> 12:53.529
Yeah.

12:55.156 --> 12:56.532
I love you too.

12:58.284 --> 12:59.952
NURSE'S OFFICE

13:00.036 --> 13:01.329
You could just cut them.

13:01.412 --> 13:03.456
Hold on.

13:04.081 --> 13:06.959
They're avoiding you for no real reason.

13:07.043 --> 13:09.462
They're a majority
singling out one person.

13:10.046 --> 13:15.092
Why bother with people
who bond over mutual hatred of others.

13:15.176 --> 13:16.177
RUMBLE RUMBLE

13:16.260 --> 13:19.096
No, it's not like that.
Sorry, I must have explained it wrong.

13:19.180 --> 13:20.723
I didn't think you'd get this mad.

13:20.806 --> 13:22.767
Of course, I'm mad.

13:22.850 --> 13:26.020
No, you're wrong! They're all nice people.

13:26.103 --> 13:27.730
I'm just not fitting in with them.

13:27.813 --> 13:31.192
Everyone has good parts to them.

13:32.652 --> 13:37.365
To say they're good people,
only to suffer when you stick with them,

13:37.448 --> 13:40.076
or to say that they helped you
that one time, so...

13:40.660 --> 13:43.371
Clinging to the good parts in people

13:44.038 --> 13:46.374
will only leave you depleted in the end.

13:47.416 --> 13:49.919
I couldn't bear to watch you
do that to yourself.

13:52.421 --> 13:53.589
WOE IS ME

13:53.673 --> 13:56.592
Miki. About before...

13:57.718 --> 14:00.846
<i>When you said,
"I don't know what I'm feeling anymore."</i>

14:01.681 --> 14:04.350
<i>I feel the same way sometimes.</i>

14:04.934 --> 14:08.688
<i>But now, whenever I look back
on the events of my day,</i>

14:08.771 --> 14:10.982
<i>if I can honestly say that I had fun,</i>

14:11.065 --> 14:14.610
<i>or that the day was truly,
honestly a good day,</i>

14:15.111 --> 14:19.323
then I think that means I must have
opened my heart to people that day.

14:21.117 --> 14:25.037
Which people bring out the "you"
that you like the most?

14:25.997 --> 14:29.917
It hurts to put yourself somewhere
where you feel like you can't be yourself.

14:30.501 --> 14:32.670
Please don't force it anymore.

14:35.798 --> 14:39.927
<i>In middle school,
I was the one causing friction.</i>

14:40.678 --> 14:45.933
<i>But then in high school, I was needed.
I was the one bringing people together.</i>

14:47.101 --> 14:48.811
<i>It felt too good to be true.</i>

14:48.895 --> 14:52.315
<i>But I wanted to protect the lie.
This fake version of myself.</i>

14:53.649 --> 14:54.734
<i>And yet...</i>

14:55.484 --> 14:57.653
Koyun. I...

14:58.654 --> 15:00.197
I want to make up with everyone.

15:02.158 --> 15:04.869
You made me realize something.

15:05.369 --> 15:08.915
I actually really like people.

15:09.916 --> 15:12.418
I like my class, and I like my classmates.

15:12.919 --> 15:16.839
I've just been faking so much
that I haven't gotten to know them.

15:17.423 --> 15:20.176
I want to start over. I want to make up.

15:20.927 --> 15:22.094
Yes.

15:22.678 --> 15:23.721
<i>Miki.</i>

15:24.722 --> 15:26.974
<i>You are too good for this world.</i>

15:30.436 --> 15:32.855
Miki didn't come.

15:36.400 --> 15:38.444
I'm going to go buy some pudding.

15:40.613 --> 15:41.614
Pudding?

15:41.697 --> 15:43.491
I'm sorry.

15:43.574 --> 15:44.784
No, you're fine.

15:47.203 --> 15:49.497
You're Miki's friend, right?

15:51.123 --> 15:53.292
Mari, Muko, and Mei.

15:53.376 --> 15:54.377
MA (MI) MU ME

15:54.460 --> 15:55.503
How do you know our names?

15:55.586 --> 15:57.380
She's told me about you.

15:57.880 --> 15:59.298
I'm a friend too.

16:00.341 --> 16:02.802
I've heard so much about you.

16:07.306 --> 16:09.308
You like sweet treats, right?

16:09.392 --> 16:11.060
QUICK, I NEED A RESTAURANT
THAT GIRLS WOULD LIKE

16:11.143 --> 16:13.479
She came with so many questions before.

16:13.562 --> 16:16.232
So that place we went to before...
Do you think...

16:16.816 --> 16:20.903
I thought she might have been
saying bad things about us.

16:21.404 --> 16:22.405
Why?

16:23.447 --> 16:27.201
Miki would never
talk behind her friends' backs.

16:27.910 --> 16:29.286
Has she ever done so in the past?

16:29.787 --> 16:31.080
I guess not.

16:31.163 --> 16:32.206
You see?

16:32.707 --> 16:35.459
And hey, what's the "Mu" in "Muko" from?

16:35.543 --> 16:36.794
KITAMURA - KITAMU - MU - MUKO

16:36.877 --> 16:39.380
- It's the "mu" from "Kitamura."
- The original is barely intact!

16:39.463 --> 16:40.464
CASUAL VIBES

16:40.548 --> 16:41.966
Well, I'm glad we cleared that up.

16:47.888 --> 16:51.267
He was actually quite friendly.

17:00.234 --> 17:01.360
Miki?

17:02.236 --> 17:06.782
There's something I'd like
to talk to you guys about after school.

17:11.245 --> 17:13.372
So...

17:14.248 --> 17:19.045
I don't think you guys have been
thinking too highly of me lately.

17:20.171 --> 17:21.172
I'm sorry.

17:21.672 --> 17:26.510
But if I'm being totally honest,
I still don't quite know what I did wrong.

17:27.470 --> 17:28.512
Still...

17:29.388 --> 17:32.016
Whether you hate me or you like me,

17:32.808 --> 17:34.685
I'd like it to be the real me.

17:37.730 --> 17:39.648
I gotta say. I...

17:39.732 --> 17:42.318
TROUBLED PAST - ACTUALLY A CRIM
I DON'T WANT TO BE AROUND YOU

17:42.401 --> 17:43.402
GULP

17:44.111 --> 17:45.654
I reinvented myself for high school.

17:48.282 --> 17:51.994
<i>I'm not at all the sweet, saccharine girl
you all think of me as,</i>

17:52.078 --> 17:53.913
<i>and I'm a far cry from being an idol.</i>

17:54.538 --> 17:57.833
I sit with my legs apart,
I kick doors shut with my feet,

17:57.917 --> 18:00.461
I forget my handkerchief
and make do by wiping my hands,

18:00.544 --> 18:02.838
and when they come to collect
my paper from up the back,

18:02.922 --> 18:06.717
my paper is always so wrinkly
from the sweat from my arms!

18:06.801 --> 18:08.761
That! That is the type of person I am!

18:08.844 --> 18:09.845
INTENSE

18:09.929 --> 18:12.098
AGAPE

18:12.181 --> 18:17.394
I thought maybe if you knew the real me
and the things I actually like,

18:17.895 --> 18:20.731
maybe you wouldn't like me so much.

18:20.815 --> 18:24.151
I've been deceiving you this whole time,
pretending to be someone I'm not.

18:25.194 --> 18:26.195
I'm sorry.

18:30.199 --> 18:36.372
I did overhear you say,
"I'm not like this at school."

18:37.581 --> 18:40.334
It made me wonder
whether you were hanging out with us

18:40.417 --> 18:42.753
despite not even wanting to be our friend.

18:42.837 --> 18:44.380
That's not true!

18:44.964 --> 18:48.634
It's just that I've been suffocating
under all these self-imposed rules.

18:49.301 --> 18:51.345
The truth is,

18:51.428 --> 18:54.765
I really do want us to be friends.

19:01.230 --> 19:04.650
We're the ones who made you
feel like you had to hold back, right?

19:05.151 --> 19:06.152
I'm sorry.

19:07.486 --> 19:08.737
GUSHING
FLUSTER FLUSTER

19:08.821 --> 19:10.656
That's not true!

19:11.323 --> 19:12.658
I'm sorry too.

19:13.367 --> 19:19.165
I believed the rumors that you
broke glass in a fight in middle school.

19:19.748 --> 19:22.501
Sorry. That one's true.

19:23.752 --> 19:24.753
FLUSTERED

19:24.837 --> 19:27.506
No, wait! I'm telling you.
I wasn't the baddie!

19:27.590 --> 19:28.799
Yes, glass broke.

19:28.883 --> 19:30.050
AND THIS AND THAT

19:30.134 --> 19:31.594
But it was more of an accident!

19:43.564 --> 19:45.065
MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

19:45.649 --> 19:47.276
How embarrassing.

19:47.359 --> 19:50.571
Miki. You're only going home now?
It's kind of late.

19:50.654 --> 19:53.199
Well, we had a lot to talk about.

19:54.074 --> 19:55.075
Right?

19:56.911 --> 19:58.704
Did you get your pudding after?

20:02.541 --> 20:03.542
INTENSE

20:03.626 --> 20:06.378
Minato! What did you do?
"After"? After what?

20:06.462 --> 20:07.588
Why does your mind go there?

20:07.671 --> 20:10.674
- Get back here!
- Calm down. Here. Cone barrier!

20:10.758 --> 20:12.843
What? A tri-cone barrier? Coward!

20:12.927 --> 20:15.596
I have never met anyone
to call it a "tri-cone" before.

20:15.679 --> 20:17.097
- Big thunder!
- Cone barrier!

20:17.181 --> 20:18.349
Miki is so...

20:18.933 --> 20:21.227
She is so funny.

20:22.811 --> 20:23.812
MIKI

20:23.896 --> 20:25.481
<i>Koyun. Thanks for today.</i>

20:25.981 --> 20:27.399
<i>I made up with everyone.</i>

20:27.900 --> 20:30.903
<i>Now I can go forth and be myself.</i>

20:30.986 --> 20:31.987
<i>Whoosh!</i>

20:36.659 --> 20:38.911
<i>Little by little, even if it's baby steps,</i>

20:39.703 --> 20:42.706
<i>I hope Miki gets to have
even more fun than she's having now.</i>

20:44.708 --> 20:45.751
So...

20:46.543 --> 20:49.255
Hi, hello!
Sorry to have caused so much worry.

20:49.838 --> 20:52.049
Well, you sure made a big change.

20:53.092 --> 20:54.510
Giving up on that idol career?

20:54.593 --> 20:57.471
Yep. I'm giving up. Yay!

20:57.972 --> 20:59.932
I mean, me? An idol? Hilarious!

21:00.015 --> 21:01.892
<i>I'm happy for you, Miki.</i>

22:33.609 --> 22:34.610
Here.

22:35.986 --> 22:38.781
Last year's end-of-school-year exams.
I got 'em.

22:38.864 --> 22:40.783
All hail Minato!

22:40.866 --> 22:43.035
Thanks, Amamiya.

22:43.118 --> 22:44.119
Sure.

22:44.203 --> 22:47.247
<i>Wait. "Sure"? Why the moody response?</i>

22:47.331 --> 22:49.041
We haven't learned these yet, have we?

22:49.124 --> 22:53.170
So for this, you use this formula,
and then you put it into this formula.

22:53.253 --> 22:55.130
Maybe we have done this before.

22:55.631 --> 22:56.673
GOT THE FUZZIES

22:56.757 --> 22:57.800
ON CLOUD NINE

23:06.850 --> 23:08.435
MIFFED

23:08.519 --> 23:09.686
SHAKE SHAKE

23:09.770 --> 23:12.314
I'm gonna go get a drink.

23:12.397 --> 23:13.398
Okay.

23:15.192 --> 23:16.610
I'll go too.

23:16.693 --> 23:18.153
Oh, sure.

23:19.196 --> 23:20.614
<i>Koyun!</i>

23:21.198 --> 23:23.450
STEP STEP

23:23.951 --> 23:26.537
Amamiya. I'm coming too.

23:27.996 --> 23:29.123
Yeah?

23:38.841 --> 23:42.219
<i>Uh-oh, what do I do? Is he in a bad mood?</i>

23:42.719 --> 23:44.805
<i>Maybe he wanted to be alone?</i>

23:44.888 --> 23:45.889
THUMP THUMP

23:46.807 --> 23:48.308
<i>Huh? What? Why?</i>

23:48.392 --> 23:49.393
THUMP THUMP

23:52.771 --> 23:54.106
- <i>So hot...</i>
- <i>So cold...</i>

23:54.189 --> 23:55.899
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
